# Network Troubleshooting Basics

## 1. Ping
Ping tests reachability using ICMP Echo messages and reports response times when replies are received. A missing reply does not always mean the destination is offline.

## 2. Traceroute
Traceroute helps identify the network hops toward a destination. Some routers may not respond to its probes, so missing hops do not necessarily indicate a fault.

## 3. Nslookup
Nslookup queries DNS records and can help troubleshoot name-resolution problems.

## Example Troubleshooting Workflow
1. Check whether the device is connected to the network.
2. Test reachability to an appropriate known destination.
3. Check DNS resolution with nslookup where a command-line environment is available.
4. Compare results and record observations before drawing conclusions.

